      "answer": "groupby() groups only consecutive identical keys; it does not sort the data. [S1](<https://pynative.com/python-itertools-functools-exercises/>)\nTo collect all equal keys together, sort by the grouping key first with sorted(data, key=...) before passing to groupby(). [S1](<https://pynative.com/python-itertools-functools-exercises/>)\ngroupby is a streaming operation that does not look ahead or back, so only adjacent elements with the same key are grouped together. [S1](<https://pynative.com/python-itertools-functools-exercises/>)",
